# build_id.pseudo
# Compile-time identity baking. Not a real build script.

ON_BUILD:
    raw = 16 cryptographically random bytes from the build host
    agent_id = format as a version-4 UUID string
    emit compiler env: AGENT_ID = agent_id

NOTE:
    The private tree greps this string out of the finished binary so the
    operator can enroll it with the relay. That recovery method is an
    OPSEC defect: anyone with the binary can derive the channel key
    (see src/channel_crypto.pseudo). This outline keeps the defect as a
    warning, not as a recipe with the original env-var name.
